    "supertram": {
      "name": "Leeds Supertram",
      "status": "abandoned",
      "description": "A three-line, 28 km light rail network with about 50 stops promoted by West Yorkshire PTE and Leeds City Council: Line 1 south to Stourton and Tingley, Line 2 north to Headingley and Bodington, Line 3 east to Seacroft and Whinmoor, meeting in a city-centre loop. Authorised by the Leeds Supertram Act 1993 and funded in 2001, it was cut back to Line 1 as costs doubled and cancelled by the government in November 2005 after about £40 million had been spent.",
